{"id":"2e181fd7-0e70-4a09-a592-fbcdc1cae421","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The 'args' parameter should be non-null during execution of 'main' as per Java runtime guarantees.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.050265Z"}
{"id":"1b5bb940-e91a-4e0b-a962-d9952e761b04","expr":"b == 0 || a / b * b + a % b == a","rationale":"If b == 0, division is not performed; otherwise, basic property of integer division and modulus ensures this holds.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.051197Z"}
{"id":"2cd52282-ff88-4d4a-8279-b21d6903ae2d","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The 'args' parameter, supplied by the JVM to main, is never null in standard usage.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.051003Z"}
{"id":"17390493-2674-4f6e-8e44-e72a12f16987","expr":"b != 0 || Integer.MIN_VALUE == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is 0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE, so this invariant is trivially always true but conveys method's documented behavior.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.051197Z"}
{"id":"b34382e5-2c6d-45f0-819c-62dfb03f598e","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"The length of an array in Java is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.050265Z"}
{"id":"c4dd8055-3cd3-48c5-aa99-76140f04ab1a","expr":"(b > 0) || (b <= 0)","rationale":"This covers all integer possibilities for b, and is useful as a partitioning fact.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.051197Z"}
{"id":"b0874f2a-1de1-4f0b-8de2-9c25f08c45ef","expr":"b == 0 ? result == Integer.MIN_VALUE : result == a / b","rationale":"Captures the method's documented behavior: if b is 0, returns MIN_VALUE, else returns integer division.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.052165Z"}
{"id":"61dff41e-7150-44a7-aa03-4c30406819de","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"All arrays in Java have a non-negative length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.051003Z"}
{"id":"3fbc0daf-0f86-4804-bd1b-241b2836fdb9","expr":"b == 0 || result == a / b","rationale":"If b is not zero, result is exactly a / b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.052165Z"}
{"id":"582146a5-68b0-4fa9-bf47-d192c871317b","expr":"a == 0 || a != 0","rationale":"This partitions the input space regarding 'a'; while tautological, it helps coverage analysis.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.051197Z"}
{"id":"7bc9566e-8d55-4535-8d2b-8302adc0eba6","expr":"b == 0 || b * result <= a && a < b * (result + 1)","rationale":"If b != 0, result is integer division so this gives the mathematical bounds for a in integer division.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.052165Z"}
{"id":"07861c61-fd72-4432-9cc0-f94022159e24","expr":"args.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"The 'args' variable is always a Java array.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.051003Z"}
{"id":"9889ad83-36b6-4fd1-aa1f-f9541205c386","expr":"b != 0 || result == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is zero, result must be Integer.MIN_VALUE.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.052165Z"}
{"id":"e0702e83-acb8-42fa-8332-94988fcc6ee8","expr":"b == 0 || Math.abs(result) <= Math.abs(a)","rationale":"If b != 0, division reduces the magnitude or keeps it the same.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:43.052165Z"}
